# Changes in reverse chronological order
#
# 0.64 Oct 25 2026 -  settings moved out of lib/ into ~/.config/botwikiawk/settings (or the file named by the environment
#                       variable BOTWIKIAWK_SETTINGS). The files in lib/ are no longer edited, by you or by setup.sh, so
#                       BotWikiAwk can be updated with git pull without losing anything. See SETUP and the top of lib/syscfg.awk.
#                       This is a breaking change for existing users:
#                         . if you edited lib/syscfg.awk or lib/botwiki.awk, git pull will refuse to overwrite them. Note your
#                           values, run "git checkout lib/syscfg.awk lib/botwiki.awk", pull, and put them in the settings file:
#                             Exe["wget"] = "/usr/bin/wget"            -->  Exe.wget  /usr/bin/wget
#                             Agent = "..." / StopButton = "..."       -->  Agent ...  /  StopButton ...
#                             case "mybot": Home = "/x/" ... in botwiki -->  bot.mybot.home  /x/   (and bot.mybot.agent)
#                         . or run ./setup.sh again - it creates the settings file with the Exe[] paths it finds, and
#                           adds only keys that are missing, so it is safe to re-run
#                         . a stop button is now off unless StopButton is set. A bot that set StopButton = "" to skip the
#                           global one should now set StopButton = "none"
#                       a value can be read from a file with file:/path, eg. "Exe.to_email file:/home/me/.secrets/to.email",
#                         so the settings file need hold no email address
#                       new lib/local.awk for your own functions, loaded by syscfg.awk into every program. It ships empty
#                         and BotWikiAwk never changes it, so git pull leaves your copy alone. If you added functions to
#                         lib/syscfg.awk (or another lib/ file), move them there
#                       lib/syscfg.awk works without setup.sh: defaults are command names found on PATH. Optional tools
#                         (mailx, parallel, lynx, wdiff) default to "" = not installed
#                     botwiki.awk: hooks so a program can extend it without editing it - readprojectcfgLocal(),
#                       setProjectPre(pid) and setProjectPost(pid) are called if the program defines them
#                     http2var(): a URL over 4000 chars is passed to wget in a file. Optional Http2varFast (no wget retries,
#                       2m cap per try) and Http2var404 (give up on a 404)
#                     getwikisource(): handles the <redirect title=".."> form, strips #section from the target, and reports
#                       a redirect with no target. A page under 150 chars is fetched again via Special:Export
#                     upload(): optional BotUser (the bot's account name, obeyed in {{bots|deny=}}) and DiscoveredTimestamp.
#                       lang defaults to "en". Debug output goes to stderr
#                     stopbutton(): retry waits can be set with StopButtonWaits
#                     sendlog() ignores an empty log name; whatistempid() uses Project["indextemp"] if it exists
#                     mkdir(): a failure is reported instead of stopping the program (it called StdErr(), which doesn't exist)
# 0.63 Feb 13 2026 -  improved http2var() and urldecodeawk(). Improved Agent and Wget_opts
# 0.62 Aug 16 2025 -  changed how SMTP authentication works. See function email() in library.awk for email cfg instructions
#                     various other minor fixes
# 0.61 Jan 16 2024 -  minor fixes
# 0.60 Dec 15 2023 -  overhaul of botwiki.awk - bot configuration is now within each bot at a BEGIN{} section near the top.
#                       This is a breaking change for existing user. See ~/example-bots for how it now looks in some sample bots.
#                       You can optionally use the old location in botwiki.awk, or mix and match. See SETUP file for instructions.
#                     create syscfg.awk moving Exe[""] definitions there so one can "@include library" without needing "@include botwiki"
#                     add support in upload() for multiple WMF projects (wikibooks, etc) and languages
#                     deprecate support for Toolforge concurrency Engines, due to drop of support for the Grid on Toolforge
#                     add support for email() in library.awk - send emails with curl via a SMTP relay server
#                     add 'auniq' to ~/bin - an alternative to uniq that doesn't require pre-sorting and maintains orig sort order
#                     fix minor bugs in library.awk
# 0.51 May 30 2021 - add some new functions to library.awk, various other updates
# 0.50 Jun 18      - add "if(Engine != 3)" to botwiki.awk removing need for project-specific customizations in this location
# 0.49 Mar 26      - add zotkill.pl for file locking ability on Toolforge
#                     improve concurrency functions for Toolforge - JobArray engine now preferred 
#                     add parallelWrite() 
# 0.47 Mar 17      - adjust randomnumber() in driver.awk
#                     add "Flush Grid buffers" to runbot.awk
#                     add gsubi() to library.awk
#                     remove infalte() and deflate() from skeleton-templates.awk (now in botwiki.awk) 
# 0.45 Feb 09 2019 - rewrite inflate() and deflate() (see code notes)
#                     fix wc()
